fs.writeFileSync(site+'/docs/FOREHEAD_NERVE_ULTRASOUND.md',`# Forehead nerve ultrasound drafts\n\nFour exact source selections share two short original lessons: the bilateral supraorbital and supratrochlear nerves. Only Ultrasound changes. The source guard binds the complete displayed identity and geometry, source file hash, node and bundle. Existing model assets and attribution remain unchanged.\n\n## Evidence and editorial limits\n\n- [Bink et al., 2023](https://doi.org/10.1097/GOX.0000000000005343): volunteer ultrasound feasibility; selected sites and either side measured. Read as acquisition-specific evidence, not a bilateral whole-course survey or diagnostic validation. The repeated notch wording in its SON/STN table is not adopted as proof of a shared anatomical exit.\n- [Berchtold et al., 2017](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28712884/): anatomical and ultrasound investigation of the named nerves. The accessible abstract does not establish a separate ultrasound sample count or per-image verification. Only the abstract was verified for this source.\n\nNo figures, tables or article text are bundled. Bink's publication has CC BY-NC-ND terms and is not admitted as a reusable image asset. The original lesson prose cites findings; no article licence is represented as commercial asset clearance. No new dependency, font, texture, scan or dataset was added.\n\n## Review\n\nConfirm the selected-source identity, the scope of superficial ultrasound examples and clinical wording against these references. The mesh is not a validated patient image; no small-branch, full-course, diagnostic or registration claim follows. Radiologist decisions remain revision-bound and independent of model/geometry review. No prior decision transfers to the changed teaching revision.\n`,{flag:'wx'});
